notes=("Kept all five old kinds; added Tansu and Bandaji. Wardrobe: armoire, linen press, kas, chifforobe as t; IKEA trimmed to 5 old ranges (PAX first). "
"Chest of drawers: tallboy/highboy/lowboy/commode/mule chest as t plus three sourced archetypes (Highboy, Commode, Mule chest). Nightstand cut from 9 to 6 IKEA ranges. "
"Blanket chest: cassone and Lane cedar chest archetypes. Trunk: dropped six Sierra Living Concepts SKU names (retail noise); added LV, Goyard, Moynat archetypes and maker-free dome-top/steamer/wardrobe trunks. "
"Left out: non-IKEA tier brands and test winners (none retrieved); Pyongan/Pakdong bandaji (only dealer search snippets); Shaker/Biedermeier/Gustavian named pieces (pages give no chest specifics; covered by traditions register). "
"Mizuya-dansu is a kitchen chest and could also cross-link to Sideboards. Kind sources switched from the Google product taxonomy to retrieved Wikipedia pages.")
